# addSelectedRows

`addSelectedRows` keeps track of selected items in the table. Works with sub-rows.

## Options

<Admonition type="info">Options passed into <code>addSelectedRows</code>.</Admonition>

```ts {3}
const table = createTable(data, {
  select: addSelectedRows({ ... }),
});
```

### `initialSelectedDataIds?: Record<string, boolean>`
Initial selected row data ids (by `row.dataId`). Default `{}`.

### `linkDataSubRows?: boolean`
Link parent/sub-row selection when updating. Default `true`.

## Column Options

<Admonition type="info">Options passed into column definitions.</Admonition>

```ts {7}
const columns = table.createColumns([
  table.column({
    header: 'Name',
    accessor: 'name',
    plugins: {
      select: { ... },
    },
  }),
]);
```

## Prop Set

<Admonition type="info">Extensions to the view model. Read <code>current.props</code> on table components, or subscribe to <code>.props()</code>. The lists below are generated from the plugin's TypeScript prop-set type, so they match the published package exactly.</Admonition>

<PluginProps set="SelectedRowsPropSet" pluginKey="select" />

## Interactions

- `allPageRowsSelected` and `somePageRowsSelected` are scoped to the current page from `addPagination`, not the whole data set. Use `allRowsSelected` for the entire table.
- The page-scoped stores read the view model's `pageRows` store, which is only populated while something subscribes to it. In a template that is always the case; in tests or headless code, subscribe to `vm.pageRows` (or read `vm.current.pageRows`) before setting `allPageRowsSelected`.
- With `addSubRows`, selecting a parent selects its sub-rows, and `someSubRowsSelected` / `allSubRowsSelected` on the parent reflect the children's state.

## Plugin State

<Admonition type="info">State provided by <code>addSelectedRows</code>.</Admonition>

```ts {3}
const vm = table.createViewModel(columns);
const { pluginStates } = vm;
const { ... } = pluginStates.select;
```

### `selectedDataIds: Writable<Record<string, boolean>>`
### `allRowsSelected: Writable<boolean>`
### `someRowsSelected: Readable<boolean>`
### `allPageRowsSelected: Writable<boolean>`
### `somePageRowsSelected: Readable<boolean>`
### `getRowState: (row) => SelectedRowsRowState`

